From: martinsngr <martin.sinegre@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 12:19:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] C fix: momentum drag from the linear face mobility

Drag in a porous cell is the average of 1/Mf over its faces, so the upwinded
kr of C also changed the momentum equation of porous cells next to free
fluid. Dragf now uses the linearly interpolated mobility, as before C; the
upwinding only enters the Darcy fluxes (porous-porous faces).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 hybridPorousInterFoam/updateVariables.H | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/hybridPorousInterFoam/updateVariables.H b/hybridPorousInterFoam/updateVariables.H
index a3f1280..2668273 100755
--- a/hybridPorousInterFoam/updateVariables.H
+++ b/hybridPorousInterFoam/updateVariables.H
@@ -7,6 +7,11 @@ kr2=krModel->kra();
 kr1f = fvc::interpolate(kr1,"kr1");
 kr2f = fvc::interpolate(kr2,"kr2");
 
+// Momentum drag keeps the original (linear) face mobility, so that the
+// upwinding below does not change the momentum equation of porous cells next
+// to free fluid (porous/free interface)
+const surfaceScalarField MfLinear(k0f*(kr1f/mu1 + kr2f/mu2));
+
 // Porous faces: kr of the upstream cell of each phase's Darcy flux (last
 // alphaEqn.H), as impesFoam (kra upwind phia, krb upwind phib). Linear
 // interpolation halves the water mobility of the face between a wet and a
@@ -32,7 +37,7 @@ Mf = M1f+M2f;
 Lf = L1f+L2f;
 
 // Calculating Drag Coefficient
-Dragf =1./Mf;
+Dragf =1./MfLinear;
 Drag= fvc::average(Dragf)*Solid;
 
 // Updating Capillary Pressure Model
